## general refactor (WE ARE DOING IT)
- easy mode dedup fixes
- deeper architectureal stuff
- study vt100 protocol to understand REPL and escape codes

### reading the code
- src/shell.ts → the primary interface (interactive + piped)
- src/bridge-loop.ts → Bridge class, the central abstraction everything talks to
- src/backend.ts → Backend interface contract (short, defines the shape)
- src/bridge.ts → claude-code backend (claude -p wrapper, NDJSON parsing)
- Commands: src/commands.ts (slash commands like /model, /prompt)
- State: src/state.ts (config, sessions, usage tracking)
- Server mode: src/server.ts → src/protocol.ts
- Tools: src/tools.ts (tool definitions for non-claude-code backends)
- Shell utilities: src/shell-utils.ts (permissions, formatting)

